<Layout
  title="About — CFL Negotiation List Tracker"
  description="This site provides independent tracking and analysis of each CFL team's Negotiation List."
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    This site provides independent tracking and analysis of each CFL team's <strong>Negotiation List</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>What Is a Negotiation List?</h2>
  <p>From the CFL:</p>
  <blockquote>
    Each CFL team maintains a Negotiation List of up to 45 players who are currently either
    unsigned or are playing in the NFL, in another professional league, or in college. Teams
    hold exclusive CFL negotiating rights with players on their lists, and those players can
    be added, traded or removed at any time.
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    Previously, these lists were infamously secretive <a href="https://press.cfl.ca/cfl-negotiation-lists-fully-unveiled" target="_blank" rel="noopener">until July 2025</a>, when the league required that they be made public and viewable through the <a href="https://stats.cfl.ca/neg-list" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CFL website</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p>
    Built and maintained by a CFL fan and data scientist <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/modalshift.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Charlie Henry</a> (go Bombers). DMs are always open.
  </p>
</Layout>
